# The old-channel thread and the injury rescue. Arc, owners and plants:
# content/STORY_BIBLE.md (spoilers). Voice: content/STYLE.md.
# Thread owners (`who ow_*`) are cast once per voyage and never overlap.

card m_carrier
type event
cat mystery
clue core
due
once
days 15 19
roles A
when !is A ow_list
when !is A ow_song
when !is A ow_garden
when !is A ow_letter
when !is A ow_dose
text {A}'s ship-to-ship receiver still scans the old common channel, which nothing on Earth listens to. It logs a carrier too faint to lock: power in a channel, no Doppler to read. Folded at 10.96 seconds, 2.4 percent duty, it stands up like a fence post. "An alias," {A} says. "Something of ours."
do who ow_hail A
do mark t_carrier

card m_alias
type event
cat mystery
clue
due
once
days 18 19
roles A B
when is A ow_hail
when since t_carrier >= 3
text {A} asks {B} to fold the same channel on {B}'s own receiver, against {B}'s own clock. An alias of something aboard would come out at a different period on a different ship. It comes out at 10.96 seconds, to the millisecond. "Not us," {A} tells the fleet channel. "Ignore my last."
do bond A B 3
do open dec_signal

card dec_signal
type decision
cat mystery
days 18 19
weight 1
once
duration 2
roles A B
lean curious open log
when fired m_alias
text Whatever the carrier is, it isn't the fleet's. {A} wants to answer it: set the receiver to reply to every burst, automatically, quoting each one's header back. {B} points out that every reply ties up the comms computer, and the letters from home queue behind a conversation with a machine.
option open | Answer every burst | {A} adds one line to the comms schedule: answer every burst on the old channel, quote it back, until someone says stop. The first answer goes out at 14:02. Then static. The carrier comes and goes as before, and {A} logs every answer to the millisecond, out of habit.
  set signal_answered
  mark t_signal
  morale B -3
  trait A curious 5
option log | Log it, keep going | The carrier goes into the anomaly log under "later". {A} tapes a printout of the folded trace above the bunk, just in case, and the comms computer stays on the letters.
  set signal_ignored
  mark t_signal
  morale A -5

card signal_reply
type event
cat mystery
due
once
days 28 31
roles A
when flag signal_answered
when is A ow_hail
text At 03:12 the receiver catches half a frame of housekeeping on the old channel, in a format nobody flies now, cut off a byte before the field that says who sent it. Since the answers started, the carrier's beat runs a few milliseconds long. Mission Control replies eight minutes later: "say again."
do trait A curious 4

card signal_echo
type event
cat mystery
due
once
days 28 31
roles A
when flag signal_ignored
when is A ow_hail
text {A} pulls the old-channel carrier out of the receiver logs again, unasked. It's stronger now, the way anything gets louder as you close on it, and its period hasn't moved by a millisecond. The anomaly report uses the word "persistent", and leaves it there. {A} keeps the printout up.
do morale A -3

# Injury and rescue: needs supplies from another ship.
card crisis_eva
type event
cat grim
once
days 10 34
weight 6
roles A
when cond A ok
when kit_elsewhere A
text A micrometeoroid hits the hull during {A}'s scheduled EVA, close enough to feel through the boots, with a suited crewmate watching from the next ship's hatch. {A} secures every tool, works back along the tether hand over hand, and comes inside with a wrist that won't bend.
do cond A injured
do who eva_who A
do morale A -10
do open rescue_kit

card rescue_kit
type rescue
cat grim
duration 1
roles A B
default volunteer
when cond A injured
when bestbond B A
text {A} needs the ultrasound and splint set from another ship's medical kit, and the next scheduled transfer window is days away.
option send | Send the kit | The fleet holds formation tight for an unscheduled transfer, and the kit rides the line across alone. {A}'s wrist is scanned and splinted by lunch, and the anomaly report runs to four pages.
  kit A
  res fuel -1
  morale A 6
option volunteer | {B} brings it over | {B} rides the line across with the kit in an unscheduled window and splints the wrist personally. The mission log calls it "nominal". Six ships read the log, and every one of them knows better.
  kitfrom B A
  move B A
  res fuel -1
  bond A B 12
  morale B 4
